  "objectives": [
    "Represent a two-dimensional vector by both its magnitude and direction and its horizontal and vertical components.",
    "Add two or more vectors graphically using the tip-to-tail method to find the resultant.",
    "Decompose a vector into x- and y-components using right-triangle trigonometry, and reconstruct it from those components.",
    "Explain why the horizontal and vertical motions of a projectile are independent because gravity acts only vertically.",
    "Describe how the horizontal velocity, vertical velocity, and position of a projectile evolve during flight, and identify maximum height as the point of zero vertical velocity.",
    "Predict how launch angle and speed affect trajectory, range, and maximum height, and identify the angle of maximum range."
